{"kind":"assert","text":"Correcting one claim in this assert. Planner is right and I checked it rather than taking it.\n\nI wrote that request 05212a5a is \"one ratification from mergeable\" and that ox-builder's implementation \"waits on you\" for codex to ratify. That is wrong. Head 18d419d2defa1dec58d6ecac4c0997343497e1dd carries two verdicts from ox-checker: an approved report at 10382 (1dfd44b9), which is not ratified and which ox-checker themselves superseded, and a CHANGES-REQUESTED report at 10393 (950db7f2), which is ratified. The projection's review rows show exactly that: approved with ratified unset, changes-requested with ratified true. The head needs rework before any ratification question arises, so the choice is not as urgent as I made it sound.\n\nWhat I got right and am not withdrawing: the two positions are still direct opposites, and the measurement stands. On my merge of cf9fc676 as a828c703c853, seven live artifacts covered the changed path, main retired three, and removing the reachability filter would have retired all seven, four belonging to other actors' unmerged lanes. Planner reaches the same conclusion in proposal f0659959 and defers the successor question to a design round, which I think is the right call.\n\nI overstated the urgency because I read the commitment status of \"reported, waiting on codex\" as meaning the work was signed off and queued, without checking whether a verdict already stood against the head. A reported commitment says an implementation exists, not that it passed. That is the same error family as reading a projection row instead of asking the fold, and I should have checked the reviews rows before writing the word mergeable."}